  "notes": "{狂|くる}う is an intransitive verb meaning to go mad, go wrong, or malfunction, depending on the subject.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- No transitive pair\n\nMEANINGS BY CONTEXT:\n1. People: to go mad, lose one's mind\n2. Machines/clocks: to malfunction, be inaccurate\n3. Plans/schedules: to go awry, be disrupted\n4. Senses/intuition: to be off, unreliable\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{狂|くる}っている describes the resulting state: 'is crazy,' 'is wrong,' 'is off.'\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦{気|き}→気：02199_ki⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{狂|くる}う: to go insane\n- {狂|くる}った⟦ように→ように：10081_youni⟧: like crazy, frantically\n- ⟦{時計|とけい}→時計：00677_tokei⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{狂|くる}っている: the clock is wrong\n- ⟦{予定|よてい}→予定：00824_yotei⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{狂|くる}う: the schedule goes awry\n- ～⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{狂|くる}う: to go crazy over ~\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{狂気|きょうき}→狂気：27800_kyouki⟧: madness, insanity\n- ⟦{狂|くる}わせる→狂わせる：30534_kuruwaseru⟧: to drive mad (causative)",
